data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" specific molecule—usually a protein or a sugar—located on the surface of a pathogen. Think of the antigen as the","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" unique \"signature\" or \"uniform\" of a germ. Your immune system uses these signatures to distinguish between \"self\"","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" (your own healthy cells) and \"non-self\" (foreign invaders).\n\nWhen a virus enters your body,","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" your immune system scans for these foreign signatures. If it finds one, it triggers an immune response. The problem is that","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" some viruses replicate so quickly that by the time your body recognizes the signature and builds a custom defense, the damage is already","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" done.\n\n#### Different Ways to Train\n\nVaccines use various methods to introduce these antigens to the body safely. The","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" goal is always the same: show the immune system the \"signature\" without causing the disease.\n\n1.  **","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"Inactivated Vaccines:** These use a version of the germ that has been killed (inactivated) using chemicals, heat,","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" or radiation. Because the germ is dead, it cannot replicate or cause disease, but its structure remains intact enough for the","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" immune system to recognize it.\n2.  **Live-Attenuated Vaccines:** These use a weakened form of","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" the germ. It is still \"alive\" and can replicate slightly, but it is too weak to cause illness in healthy","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" people. This provides a very strong, long-lasting response because it closely mimics a natural infection.\n3.  ","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"**Subunit, Recombinant, and Conjugate Vaccines:** Instead of using the whole germ, these vaccines use only a","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" tiny, specific piece of it—like a single protein or a piece of its outer shell. This is highly targeted and","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" carries very little risk.\n4.  **mRNA Vaccines:** This is a newer, revolutionary technology. Instead of injecting","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" a piece of the germ, mRNA vaccines provide your cells with a \"blueprint\" (messenger RNA). Your own cells read","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" this blueprint to temporarily produce a harmless piece of the antigen (like a spike protein). Your immune system sees this protein,","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" recognizes it as foreign, and begins the training process.\n\n#### The Training Process: Recognition and Response\n\nOnce the vaccine","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" introduces the antigen, a multi-step biological process begins. First, specialized cells called **dendritic cells** act","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":" as scouts. They ingest the antigen and \"present\" it to other immune cells, effectively shouting, \"Look at this","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"! This doesn't belong here!\"\n\nThis alert activates two main branches of the adaptive immune system:\n\n*   ","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":1,"delta":{"text":"**B-cells:** These are the \"weapon manufacturers.\" Once activated, B-cells produce **antibodies**—Y","type":"text"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

